@title User Guide: Prototype Applications
@group userguide

Information about prototypes.

Overview
========

Phorge includes some //prototype applications//, which are applications in an
early stage of development.

Prototype application are not enabled by default. You can use the
`phabricator.show-prototypes` configuration setting to enable prototypes.

//Using// Prototype applications is generally //not supported// - we won't help
if you try to use them and something breaks. Since the Phorge organization does
not offer paid support, this is technically true for all other applications, but
we would feel sorry for you and try to help if it's non-prototype.

Historically, Prototype phase was used as an early way to test the
implementation and integration of a new application without committing to
support it. This allowed us to get a better sense of how the application
might work and integrate with other applications, and what technical and product
challenges it might face.

This concept no longer works for us, as new applications are not expected to be
implemented in the Core repository.

Some of the Prototypes are slated for removal, and some are being promoted to
non-prototype status. Some will be removed from Core and move to their own
Extension library. See [[https://we.phorge.it/T16277 |T16277 Eliminate concept
of "prototype application" ]] for updates on this front.
